            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Louis J. Rovelli, Pennsylvania\u2019s policy restricts newspapers, magazines, and photographs for a small class of dangerous, disruptive inmates confined at level\u202f2 of the Long Term Segregation Unit, the most restrictive custody level in the state prison system."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Souter",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5de83145e39d3d844a18df824ff0bd6b426a679b73bd84b2a4bd96e84bb7109e",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5de83145e39d-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Souter questioned whether the policy implicates First Amendment rights, asking if the analysis should be treated similarly to the Eighth Amendment analysis."
      }
    ],
